With negligible initial speed and no height change,
\[
\Delta p=\frac{1}{2}\rho v^2
\]
\[
v=\sqrt{\frac{2\Delta p}{\rho}}
=\sqrt{\frac{2(18\times10^3)}{1000}}
=6.0\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}
\]

The stagnation pressure rise is the dynamic pressure:
\[
\Delta p=\frac{1}{2}\rho v^2
\]
\[
v=\sqrt{\frac{2\Delta p}{\rho}}
=\sqrt{\frac{2(540)}{1.2}}
=30\,\mathrm{m\,s^{-1}}
\]

The pressure energy per volume becomes gravitational potential energy per volume:
\[
p_{\mathrm{gauge}}=\rho gh
\]
\[
h=\frac{p_{\mathrm{gauge}}}{\rho g}
=\frac{45\times10^3}{(1000)(9.8)}
=4.6\,\mathrm{m}
\]
